private/
.claude/
*.oldturd
*.tmp
*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime output of the work-record hooks, produced by running the tests and by
# the guards themselves. `state/` holds task files; `worklog/` holds the prompt
# history and the audit trail. Both are machine state, neither is source, and
# the history contains whatever Bob typed. This repo is public.
hooks/state/
hooks/worklog/

# Model-panel review output. Verdicts land in the project the run was about,
# and they are large, per-run, and reproducible from the bundle. Not source.
.regents/

# Scratch space. Anything in here that turns out to matter gets filed properly
# in the project; the README is tracked so the directory always exists.
temp/*
!temp/README.md

# Reading material: scraped articles kept for reference while designing the
# work agreement. Someone else's writing, some of it paywalled, and this repo
# is public. Stays local.
library/

# Working documents rather than source. The decision-and-undo brief is written
# for one reader and regenerated when the design changes.
*.docx
